Description: graphical editor for the GRUB boot loader configuration
 Mainuan GRUB Editor is a GTK 3 application to edit /etc/default/grub and
 the GRUB appearance without a text editor:
  * timeout, default entry and default boot mode, screen resolution and
    kernel parameters;
  * boot entries: enable, disable or remove memtest and custom entries,
    and add custom entries to /etc/grub.d/40_custom;
  * themes, background image, colours and fonts (TTF/OTF converted with
    grub-mkfont).
 .
 The editor runs as root through pkexec and calls update-grub to apply the
 changes. The interface is translated and follows the language of the
 KDE Plasma session.
